Z||000000||justme||05-31-2001||03:02 PM||||hello<P>i have an 87 se v6 2.8 with auto transmission. <P>the car won't go into park unless shifted into park while the car is still slightly moving forward. when it doesn't go into park, i have to start the car in neutral or nothing happens.  <P>when i shift back from park to reverse it completely skips over it and feels very mushy, with the first click occurring at neutral. then, if i shift back up from neutral it will go into reverse every time no problem.<P>right before i lost reverse and park, i couldn't shift down into gears 1 and 2, the shifter would just stop like it was against the end of the shift board? these work now that i lost reverse and park though.<P>i checked the trans. fluid levels - ok.  i had all the seals replaced and the tranny flushed when i rebuild my engine just over a year ago.  also, the new shift stick in the handle (resembles a bubbly plastic straw) bends when i push the button on the shift handle rather than engaging the transmission.<P>any thoughts would be a great help. thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||05-31-2001||03:14 PM||||Sounds like the cable has gone sloppy or is out of adjustment. Check the brackets and make sure every thing is tight and that the cable is locked in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||05-31-2001||05:32 PM||||Also, make sure that the shifter is on in the correct spot. <BR>I replaced mine once and i had it down too far and it acted a little like you're saying. I took it off again, then put it back right and it was fine.||||reg||1
